GAL22V10
RoctecUA4


AB16 AB17 AB18 AB19 AB20 AB21 AB22 AB23 STRAP0 STRAP1 STRAP2 GND
/EN  NC   /AS  DBX  DB14 DBY   CLK1 BANK STRB DLY  NC     VCC


; ============================================================
;   UA4 GAL22V10 - Draft 05 (restored as known-safe baseline)
; ============================================================
;
;   This is the "broken-chip emulator" we confirmed boots the
;   Amiga cleanly (card invisible to autoconfig). All UA4
;   outputs are at safe defaults:
;
;     CLK1 - constant HIGH (no edges to U14)
;     STRB - constant HIGH (no edges to U12 / UA6)
;     DLY  - constant HIGH (C1 charges to VCC)
;     DB14 - permanent Hi-Z
;     DBX  - permanent Hi-Z (no R11 / UA6 contention)
;     DBY  - permanent Hi-Z (no R15 / UA6 contention)
;
;   /AS and BANK inputs referenced via tautological
;   contradictions in DBX.E and DBY.E so GALasm marks pins 15
;   and 20 as INPUT, not NC.
;
;   What we learned during Draft 06-08 attempts (and why we
;   reverted to Draft 05):
;
;     - Draft 06 (CLK1 active LOW pulse on $E8+/AS): /OVR
;       asserts during $E8 reads but no /DTACK comes back -
;       CPU stalls forever waiting for the cycle to complete.
;       /AS stays LOW, our CLK1 stays LOW as a consequence,
;       /OVR stays LOW because U14 never gets a release edge.
;
;     - Draft 07 (+ STRB active LOW pulse): U12 evolves under
;       STRB=LOW into a steady state where its IO7 output goes
;       LOW and stays LOW. That's U11's CLK input - now stuck.
;       U11 never advances state, never asserts /DTACK. Same
;       hang at grey screen.
;
;     - Draft 08 (STRB polarity inverted, active HIGH): worse
;       than Draft 07 - red screen now, meaning U12/U11/UA6
;       cascade lands in a state that disrupts the chipset.
;
;   Conclusion: without the actual fuse maps of U11, U12, UA6
;   (and ideally U14) we cannot predict what UA4 outputs need
;   to look like for the cascade to come up correctly. The
;   Galdurino-based fuse dump is now the prerequisite next
;   step. Once we have U11/U12/UA6/U14 equations, this draft
;   gets replaced with one that actually drives the autoconfig
;   handshake properly.
; ============================================================


; --- Always-driven HIGH outputs (no tri-state) ---
CLK1 = VCC
STRB = VCC
DLY  = VCC


; --- Always-Hi-Z outputs (tri-state with enable forced FALSE) ---
;     Contradictions in .E force AS and BANK to INPUT mode.
DB14.T = VCC
DB14.E = AB16 * /AB16

DBX.T = VCC
DBX.E = AS * /AS

DBY.T = VCC
DBY.E = BANK * /BANK


DESCRIPTION

UA4 GAL22V10 Draft 05 (restored): "broken-chip emulator".
Confirmed safe baseline - boots the Amiga, card invisible.
Drafts 06-08 attempts to enable real behavior failed because
we don't know the U11 / U12 / UA6 / U14 fuse maps. Next step
is Galdurino fuse dumps; this draft is the known-good
checkpoint to come back to.
